**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Vietnam Poverty and Equity Assessment - From the Last Mile to the Next Mile","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-04-28","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/vietnam/publication/2022-vietnam-poverty-and-equity-assessment-report","claim":"Vietnam's LMIC poverty rate fell from 16.8% to 5% over 2010-2020, more than 10 million people escaped poverty, but COVID-19 halted wage growth and the social protection system still struggled to reach informal workers.","locator":"Main messages, lines 56-65 and policy recommendations lines 75-83","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank country assessment with explicit summary statistics and policy analysis; strong for baseline and remaining gaps, though not direct ruler-order evidence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Country-level baseline and inherited trajectory relevant to 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect only. Reflects long-run system performance, predecessor reforms, and the 2022 policy environment; not a direct record of one personally ordered act by Nguyễn Phú Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["The report says COVID-19 set back progress and social protection reach remained incomplete.","The same report calls for more effective social assistance and higher coverage/benefit levels."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF Viet Nam Key Results 2022","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/unicef-viet-nam-key-results-2022","claim":"UNICEF says it worked with 12 national and six local partners in 2022, focusing on the most vulnerable children and families while delivering results across health, protection, nutrition, water, sanitation, clean environment, education, and social protection.","locator":"Intro and situation sections, lines 71-79 and 169-174","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct UNICEF country-report summary of 2022 programming and implementation, but some claims are program-output oriented and partly donor-supported.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about 2022 and the target period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful. The work was done with Vietnamese ministries and local partners under the 2022 country-program framework; it does not by itself prove personal direction from Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["UNICEF also says many children were still at risk of being left behind.","The page itself notes major disparities remained a challenge."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.5","6B.6","6B.8","6B.9","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Study on Multidimensional child poverty in Viet Nam","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam and the General Statistics Office","publication_date":"2022-12","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/documents/study-multidimensional-child-poverty-viet-nam-2022","claim":"UNICEF and GSO say children are a vulnerable group and that deprivations in nutrition, education, sanitary toilets, and clean water damage children's health and education throughout life.","locator":"Highlights, lines 73-74","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Joint UNICEF-GSO publication directly focused on child poverty and multidimensional deprivation in Vietnam.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Uses updated data through 2020 and frames the 2022 policy problem space.","ruler_attribution":"Country-condition evidence only; it does not isolate Trọng's personal contribution, but it is relevant to the inherited welfare baseline he governed in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["The document is diagnostic rather than an implementation evaluation.","It does not quantify ruler-specific gains in 2022."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Health","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/health","claim":"UNICEF says around 30,000 under-five children in Vietnam die each year from avoidable and treatable diseases, and births remain unsafe especially for women and babies from ethnic groups and hard-to-reach areas.","locator":"Challenges section, lines 93-94 and 105-113","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNICEF country-program page with clear, specific burden estimates; not a government administrative record but credible for baseline and gaps.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Target-period context and inherited baseline; not a 2022 event-specific outcome report.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. This describes structural health-system conditions under the party-state, not a discrete instruction from Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["The same page also notes more infants survive to age five than before and fewer women die in childbirth.","It does not isolate 2022 policy attribution."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Education","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/education","claim":"UNICEF says Vietnam's education system remains unequal: just under half of rural children and one-third of the poorest households complete upper secondary education, while only one-in-10 children with disabilities attends secondary school and one-in-five ethnic minority students reach upper secondary or higher.","locator":"Challenges section, lines 80-86","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNICEF country page with concrete inequality claims; strong on access gaps, though not a causal evaluation of one ruler's choices.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Structural 2022 baseline and near-term context.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect country-condition evidence; attributable to the regime and state capacity more than to a single named order by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["The page also says Vietnam's system has been transformational for many children.","It does not show whether 2022 reforms under Trọng reduced the gaps."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.8","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH)","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/water-sanitation-and-hygiene-wash","claim":"UNICEF says more than seven million children still lack clean water and sanitation at school, nearly three million people practice open defecation, and 16 million people lack hygienic latrines.","locator":"Challenges section, lines 92-96","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNICEF country WASH page with precise figures and a clear welfare nexus.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Structural baseline relevant to 2022 service provision and child welfare.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. This is a broad country-level service gap, not a ruler-specific operational order.","contrary_evidence":["The page also says Vietnam has made rapid progress in WASH services and support.","The figures are country-level and not directly tied to 2022 implementation by Trọng."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.8","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF Representative: Viet Nam builds strong immunization system against COVID-19","publisher":"UNICEF Viet Nam / Government News interview","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://www.unicef.org/vietnam/press-releases/unicef-representative-viet-nam-builds-strong-immunization-system-against-covid-19","claim":"UNICEF's representative said Vietnam implemented the largest-scale vaccination campaign it had attempted, built a strong immunization system, and achieved 95% second-dose coverage for adults and 94% for ages 12-17.","locator":"Interview lines 77-85 and 87-88","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct interview with UNICEF representative published by UNICEF, giving specific vaccination-performance figures and implementation claims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and tied to the pandemic response environment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant. The statement credits the Vietnamese Government and vaccine diplomacy, but it is still not a direct order from Trọng himself.","contrary_evidence":["The same interview notes Vietnam had previously struggled to secure vaccine supply.","It does not measure routine child immunization or broader service quality."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.5","6B.6","6B.9","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Tổng Bí thư Nguyễn Phú Trọng trả lời phỏng vấn nhân dịp Năm Mới 2022","publisher":"Government of Viet Nam (Báo Điện tử Chính phủ)","publication_date":"2022-01-01","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/tong-bi-thu-nguyen-phu-trong-tra-loi-phong-van-nhan-dip-nam-moi-2022-102306496.htm","claim":"Trọng said the first-year task after the Party Congress was to turn the Party's resolutions into reality, make the country rich, and bring happiness to the people, while stressing social security and people's lives as central issues.","locator":"Interview lines 184-189 and 192-195","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct statement from Trọng in a government-published interview; strong for rhetoric and stated priorities, weaker for implementation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and tied to his own words.","ruler_attribution":"Direct. This is Trọng's own 2022 articulation of governing purpose, though rhetoric alone does not prove delivery.","contrary_evidence":["The interview is programmatic and does not itself prove execution.","It is paired with regime-level claims rather than independent outcome verification."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.5","6B.9","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Tổng Bí thư Nguyễn Phú Trọng tiếp Thủ tướng New Zealand Jacinda Ardern","publisher":"Government of Viet Nam (Báo Điện tử Chính phủ)","publication_date":"2022-11-14","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/tong-bi-thu-nguyen-phu-trong-tiep-thu-tuong-new-zealand-102221114191716968.htm","claim":"Trọng said Vietnam's socio-economic achievements in 2022 had improved the people's material and spiritual life, including positive results in COVID-19 control, economic recovery, and social security.","locator":"Article line 186","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct quoted remarks from Trọng in an official government publication; good for stated priorities and self-assessment, not independent verification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct statement by Trọng, though it remains self-presentation and not an independent audit.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is celebratory and does not quantify attributable causation.","Independent sources are still needed for delivery quality and remaining gaps."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.6","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Resolution on socio-economic recovery and development program passed","publisher":"Government of Viet Nam (VGP News)","publication_date":"2022-01-11","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/resolution-on-socio-economic-recovery-and-development-program-passed-11122011117055838.htm","claim":"The National Assembly approved a recovery package that set aside VND 176 trillion to modernize grassroots health systems, disease-control centers and hospitals, plus VND 5 trillion in preferential loans through the Vietnam Bank for Social Policies and VND 46 trillion for vaccines, drugs, and medical supplies.","locator":"Lines 161-173","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government summary of a passed resolution with specific budget lines and social-service allocations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and central to 2022 crisis response.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material. The resolution was passed by the National Assembly and executed by government institutions under the party-state led by Trọng; it is not a personal directive in the source text.","contrary_evidence":["The same resolution is a policy announcement, not proof of delivery.","Implementation depended on ministries and local authorities."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.6","6B.9","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Quyết định số 08/2022/QĐ-TTg của Thủ tướng Chính phủ: Quy định về việc thực hiện chính sách hỗ trợ tiền thuê nhà cho người lao động","publisher":"Government of Viet Nam (official legal database)","publication_date":"2022-03-28","url":"https://vanban.chinhphu.vn/?docid=205538&pageid=27160","claim":"The Prime Minister's decision created housing-rental assistance for workers in industrial parks and key economic regions, including VND 500,000 per person per month for up to 3 months and VND 1,000,000 per person per month for returning workers.","locator":"Search-result summary and Decision Articles 1, 8, and 9","source_type":"legal/official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official legal text with exact eligibility, amount, and duration; strong evidence of a targeted welfare response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The decision was issued by the Prime Minister, not Trọng personally, but it fits the party-state policy direction under his leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The benefit is targeted, temporary, and limited to specific worker groups.","It does not show universal social protection expansion."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.7","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Hỗ trợ ngân sách địa phương thực hiện các chính sách an sinh xã hội","publisher":"Government of Viet Nam (Báo Điện tử Chính phủ)","publication_date":"2022-01-24","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/ho-tro-ngan-sach-dia-phuong-thuc-hien-cac-chinh-sach-an-sinh-xa-hoi-102220124174813178.htm","claim":"The central budget provided targeted support to local budgets for centrally issued social policies in 2022-2025, including increased costs from the multidimensional-poverty threshold and other social-security measures.","locator":"Lines 177-199","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government explanation of budget support rules for social-policy implementation; concrete and directly relevant to welfare delivery.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly 2022 and aimed at 2022-2025 implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful. This is system-level policy under the party-state leadership associated with Trọng, though the source does not attribute the measure to him personally.","contrary_evidence":["The measure is conditional and budget-limited rather than universal.","It shows support architecture more than outcomes."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.9","6B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 25-40 documents across official, IGO, and NGO sources and kept the ones that best covered 2022 welfare action plus the remaining gaps. Accepted sources were the World Bank poverty/equity assessment, UNICEF's 2022 Viet Nam results page, UNICEF's child poverty study, UNICEF health/education/WASH country pages, WHO's vaccination story, two direct Trọng statements, the 2022 socio-economic recovery resolution, the worker rent-support decision, and the central budget support decision for social policies.

I rejected or de-prioritized:
- Global or non-Viet Nam-only reports that were too generic for ruler-period attribution.
- Older background pages when a sharper 2022 source existed for the same claim.
- Sources focused mainly on macroeconomics or business conditions unless they had a direct social-welfare channel.
- Duplicate summaries of the same UNICEF/World Bank claims.
- 2025 retrospective items where the 2022-specific pages already supplied cleaner evidence.
- Media-only pieces when an official, UNICEF, WHO, or World Bank source covered the same point better.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct evidence on Trọng's personal role in social-service administration is still thin. Most evidence is system-level and party-state level, not a documented one-person instruction chain.
- National implementation data on social protection reach, benefit adequacy, and subgroup coverage in 2022 is still incomplete, especially for adults outside child-focused programs.
- More work would help on whether 2022 recovery and social-policy measures materially improved outcomes for the poorest quintile, ethnic minorities, and informal workers by year end rather than only on paper.
